<title>FRANCE: Matif commodities futures volume rose in June.</title>
<headline>Matif commodities futures volume rose in June.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The volume of commodities futures and options traded on the French MATIF exchange rose 92.2 percent in June from the previous month and 3.8 percent compared with June 1996, operator Matif SA said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Detailed figures for commodity contracts were as follows.</p>
<p>			 Volume    Change	Change   Open positions</p>
<p>				     on month    on year   at end-month</p>
<p> All contracts	20,139    92.2 pct     3.8 pct   12,234</p>
<p>  Total futures     19,989    90.7 pct     3.8 pct   12,134</p>
<p>of which:</p>
<p>White sugar ($)</p>
<p>    45 Icumsa sugar 12,055   114.5 pct   -22.1 pct    6,955</p>
<p>    100 Icumsa sugar 1,547	N/A	  N/A	  1,148</p>
<p>    Rapeseed	   4,597     6.6 pct    56.7 pct    2,839</p>
<p>    Wheat		1,790   226.0 pct     N/A	  1,192</p>
<p>    Sugar options	150	N/A	  N/A	    100</p>
<p>NOTE - The 100 Icumsa sugar contract began trading on June 20.</p>
<p>--Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
